  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the diversity statute defines a corporation\u2019s citizenship as the state where it has its principal place of business."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the Ninth Circuit erred in holding Hertz a citizen of California, even though Hertz is headquartered in New\u202fJersey and conducts over 80\u202fpercent of its operations outside California."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, congress intended in 1958 to preserve diversity jurisdiction for corporations in the 48 states and to deny it only in the state where the corporation\u2019s principal place of business is located."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Srinivasan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Srinivasan, respondents argue that the principal place of business should be determined by the location of the corporation\u2019s principal executive offices, as shown in its 10\u2011K report."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Schneider",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Schneider, the Ninth Circuit noted that Hertz has 43\u202fpercent more employees, 75\u202fpercent more property, and 60\u202fpercent more revenue in California than elsewhere."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Schneider",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Schneider, congress\u2019s first goal in the jurisdictional scheme was to prevent gaming of the system."
      }
